Z||000000||Jaei Sun||02-28-2001||03:04 PM||||I took out my air filter box and I noticed the smaller hose that was attached to the side of it leads to nothing.  It runs right behind the engine and when I follow where it ends, I see that it just runs to an open end.  I looked back there and couldn't see anything it attaches to.  Any one know if this is supposed to be connected to somthing?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||02-28-2001||03:21 PM||||Just a guess, but you must have a V-6??  The line you see was disconnected during one of the recalls.  It used to be the crankcase vent line connection.  The tube that plugs into the rubber boot near the throttle body is the new system.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||7
Z||000002||Jaei Sun||02-28-2001||03:24 PM||||THANKS Ron!!!  Right on about the V6!  Man I was going nuts looking thru the service manual trying to find it's function.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||02-28-2001||03:57 PM||||In case you haven't already figured it out, you want to plug that tube. It lets the engine suck unfiltered engine compartment air. The shop that did the recall was supposed to change the air box to one without that connection, but we all know that not all shops are reliable.||||reg||1
